<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>French PM brings forward hike in minimum wage to calm protesters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccb1b41196c20c63946795e88c200f426e811b7480dbe7e1c23f831eba6253ab</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:47:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters--1f3e775b1585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said ​on Monday, November 9, he was bringing forward a planned hike in the minimum wage to December from January, as he sought to defuse a cost-of-living crisis that has sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years. Unions swiftly dismissed the offer as "crumbs".</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran's Revolutionary Guards behind cyberattacks on supermarket fridges, says French FM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66a3793ef886f77bf6289598a35cdd5b0e865336c25fe07a2ee0ffd086815a41</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot--977c1baab94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot" /><summary type="html">French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country. The Paris prosecutor's office said it had opened an investigation into an Iranian cyber unit affiliated with the Guards over the cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c95e72b4062693fce9597b6a687e82fdf5420c16ee341d2b576046d449f02204</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--8261ff0a2a6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's right holds poll lead over Sanchez's Socialists ahead of November 29 snap election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d78dcf6307305474910668be5989b7b21cf40e2179d3f8220cb24d8a4fd770c</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election--1d062be0599a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's ruling Socialists have narrowed the gap but continue to trail the conservative People's Party, who would need to team up with the far-right Vox party to secure a majority of seats in parliament, pollsters say with three weeks to go before the country's general election.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Shock and grief in Poland after weekend mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f37badd7e7358bb0002f2d2ae33ac4fc277f3f8d1d2b15f0523e2a9ebecaa067</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:31:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting--e6f1c827a5aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland was in shock after a weekend mass shooting in which a gunman opened fire, killing six people and wounding 15 in the city of Krakow before police shot and wounded him. The shooter died in the hospital on Monday morning, police said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russell Brand sentenced to 10 years, 6 months for rape and sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:657a1c8220910dca846bcba44a91f29b5ce7b719940e54cfd436cb6814db276a</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:45:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault--3be1a4c1e376.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">Comedian Russell ​Brand, once one ‌of Britain's most high-profile broadcasters, ⁠was sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in prison on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and ‌sexually assaulting three more around two decades ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Saving the Venetian lagoon: A natural buffer against climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:434fe329b208f1cee2e12bb2be9483307c1a98c16899c92cbeeeca55bf0573d5</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:18:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change--0c07a9ddcfbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change" /><summary type="html">The Venetian lagoon is home to "barene" – salt marshes made of vegetation and mud, which play an important role against the effects of climate breakdown. They absorb CO2 and can store it long term in the soil, even more efficiently than land forests. But erosion and rising sea levels are threatening these natural ramparts. Today, scientists and environmental associations are trying to save these unique ecosystems. Our Italy correspondent Natalia Mendoza reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: A focus on electrification as extreme weather events shake the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a851538f9a0bad5ec92b7ba976886fa7ae7760194ba9e14da2e341ce72d312c</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:35:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-cop31-a-focus-on-electrification-as-extreme-weather-events-shake-the-world" /><summary type="html">Most of the world’s countries are gathering this week for COP31 in Antalya, Turkey. This United Nations Climate Change Conference opens amid deep concern following extreme weather events such as the deadly floods in Nepal and a supersized El Niño. Experts say that in uncertain times, it is even more important to accelerate global efforts.</summary></entry><entry><title>French policemen go on trial over 2020 beating of Black music producer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdf70b2bf1b86f959416ff2ebf99d22738593c787f933ce5b8b21fe2343d48d6</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:38:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-policemen-go-on-trial-over-2020-beating-of-black-music-producer--eb4ea46f0e38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-policemen-go-on-trial-over-2020-beating-of-black-music-producer" /><summary type="html">Three French policemen went on trial on Monday, November 9, over the beating of a Black music producer they say was not wearing a face mask during the Covid pandemic, in a rare police brutality case to go to court. The assault on Michel Zecler, now 47, triggered renewed outrage in France over police violence, which victims and researchers say is systemic.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM Lecornu holds talks over protesters' cost-of-living concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35b6c2b5e71f42441902405df885cd8c813e50c6fa26f331751fb48863c09b3c</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:40:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-holds-talks-over-protesters-cost-of-living-concerns--4e605f80054d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-holds-talks-over-protesters-cost-of-living-concerns" /><summary type="html">French Prime ⁠Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet ​representatives of employers' organisations and private-sector unions on Monday, November 9, to try ​to address cost-of-living concerns that have sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland begins 2 days of national mourning after gunman kills 6</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31dc563fc01000934b81e74f0fd8781924caf4f934d1f388db4601eb604edc60</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:37:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-poland-begins-2-days-of-national-mourning-after-gunman-kills-6--0409be610d4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-poland-begins-2-days-of-national-mourning-after-gunman-kills-6" /><summary type="html">Poland has begun two days of national mourning after a gunman opened fire in Krakow's main square Saturday afternoon, November 7. Six people were killed and at least 15 were injured. The gunman was shot and detained by police. He then died later in hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>European troops in Poland: 'Coalition of the Willing' holds military exercises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840fc74b6205508f4d0bf237b04245d986f181ea7f6ba98c303f0295edfb6db5</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T09:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-european-troops-in-poland-coalition-of-the-willing-holds-military-exercises--962b498289fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-european-troops-in-poland-coalition-of-the-willing-holds-military-exercises" /><summary type="html">Some 2,800 troops from 10 different European countries are taking part in a multinational military exercise in Poland.  The aim is to prepare European forces for a possible deployment to Ukraine after hostilities end.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Nazi vanity project': Eagle's Nest in Bavarian Alps a symbol of regime's 'conquest of nature'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9db991327ad43efc85cf285cc9ba10986da3776166d9d48ab637a408b1b2856</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T09:45:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nazi-vanity-project-eagle-s-nest-in-bavarian-alps-a-symbol-of-regime-s-conquest-of-nature--dccb3075f0ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nazi-vanity-project-eagle-s-nest-in-bavarian-alps-a-symbol-of-regime-s-conquest-of-nature" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Sir Richard Evans, British Historian and Regius Professor Emeritus of History at the University of Cambridge. The controversy surrounding the fate of Adolf Hitler's Eagle's Nest, the Nazi-era mountaintop complex in the Bavarian Alps, raises profound questions about the relationship between architecture, historical memory and political extremism. At the heart of the debate lies a difficult distinction: preserving the material evidence of history is not necessarily the same as preserving the symbols through which a criminal regime sought to glorify itself. "This is a Nazi vanity project," Evans argues and his conclusion is unequivocal: the mountain must be "restored to its natural state."</summary></entry><entry><title>'We call it war-life balance': Daryna's daily struggle to live, survive in wartime Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e46cc9254224befeea2cb908fa4b34b6a5d3252b5aa82aa205bc3d6e0450196</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T09:10:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-we-call-it-war-life-balance-daryna-s-daily-struggle-to-live-survive-in-wartime-ukraine--134901708653.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-we-call-it-war-life-balance-daryna-s-daily-struggle-to-live-survive-in-wartime-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Daryna, 25, entered adulthood in a country at war. Since Russia’s full-scale invasion, her days have been shaped by air raid alerts, power outages and nights spent sheltering in the subway. Despite the uncertainty that shadows every day, she is determined to preserve a semblance of normal life in Kyiv. FRANCE 24 met a young woman who has become emblematic of a generation learning to live under daily bombardment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland braces for tense week after deadly Krakow shooting deepens political divisions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d708ae9e056c55a6cfb9e2c6c9e0937e9f99f1bae250b550311786e7f25572d0</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T07:43:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-poland-braces-for-tense-week-after-deadly-shooting-deepens-political-divisions--c9472a1db641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-poland-braces-for-tense-week-after-deadly-shooting-deepens-political-divisions" /><summary type="html">Poland faces a week of political tensions after its deadliest shooting in decades left six people dead and dozens wounded in Krakow on Saturday. The attack has heightened concerns over rising far-right extremism ahead of a major nationalist march.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: US midterms 'Blue Wave', French protests and Dakar Youth Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adc3cebbb79bbeb95c246da02589d7547cea9c588dad69a8d4cb8059d8b7cd97</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:21:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics--c8336674c1f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics" /><summary type="html">From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffce900d82c8a3375c24b6b66ca7232a7ce62b03eacdf54f9cf2e782cb884895</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:21:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting--b5967a40cc64.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2718910934304cd891deb7bcab935f2bbc6645cd2bc5d95ad19abbd94abf7f4</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:18:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting--bd87f2f4ae08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c28c259bab2b86da87c7ad66529ffa9c981819eba05d27d212e9bece43aed095</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says--c38c48e4c7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says" /><summary type="html">France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland launches terrorism probe into mass shooting in Krakow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efc8a71ba6d2bec07a2d9952bea81ce0927599dfb4ba32f8549c37afc9fd86da</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T08:59:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting--608f97551b17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies” and died in hospital on Monday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman kills six in Krakow, three more bodies found at his house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0674b30e519aa92087aff26fbe80ccb3d1d0843b4afe8fc3504db585f2c5ea38</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T22:47:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house--dc06bdec4f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house" /><summary type="html">A chilling new discovery in Poland, where three bodies have reportedly been found inside the Krakow gunman's home. That's in addition to six people killed and sixteen wounded when the attacker opened fire in the city's historic square. Prime Minister Donald Tusk has now declared the shooting an act of terrorism, saying Poland has never experienced anything quite like it. The 25-year-old suspect, described by authorities as holding radical far-right views, was shot by police.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gunman who killed at least six in Krakow ‘fascinated’ by far-right ideologies, government says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a18761be66790e422cc09a35b03bb0d9f26b475327d9a25ae00c23ef1366182</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say--f51ffab85332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say" /><summary type="html">A gunman reportedly "fascinated by far-right ideologies" shot and killed at least six people and wounded more than a dozen in Krakow’s main market square on Saturday, Polish authorities said. Three more bodies were later found at the home of the gunman, who was wounded and taken into custody.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches massive strike on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dd7ee4d1f76c68f95c12296d16328537ecf7d64776092b6a5aa8f91f096375e</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1--1213cd3ff896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">As Ukraine prepares for another round of talks with Russia and the United States next week, Moscow has launched a massive overnight strike. At least five people were injured in Kyiv, where Russian missiles damaged residential and commercial buildings, forced the closure of a bridge over the Dnipro River and caused fresh power and water outages. Ophélie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI Data centres face growing backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa61b9ace010c53ff8959bfe652cbb7e6b50f05697eaa0828a93f2fb769e64af</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash--009b8f3b4c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash" /><summary type="html">Democrats are also calling for tighter regulation of AI data centres, a concern shared across Europe. In Amsterdam, several hundred activists occupied the site of a planned Microsoft data centre as part of a two-day protest taking place across the continent. Jennie Shin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia hits Kyiv and surrounding region in massive overnight strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03be2b890d4225e5b94abb50eddc2346eb7f9796e1362be5f4e0d2b20cbce1c0</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-moscow-strikes-kyiv-as-ukraine-prepares-for-talks-with-russia-and-the-us--a1d6ff529852.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-moscow-strikes-kyiv-as-ukraine-prepares-for-talks-with-russia-and-the-us" /><summary type="html">Moscow ⁠carried out missile ​and drone attacks on Kyiv and the surrounding region overnight Friday to Saturday, targeting energy infrastructure and killing at least one person while wounding eight, authorities said. Russia recently stepped up air strikes on ​Ukraine, worsening living conditions for residents who have limited access to power and water.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe bomb hoaxes widen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee0212fda6b7ea5b796e24e8c37d4e9d82345e80f5ece7c2d254d24066bd4919</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:22:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-bomb-hoaxes-widen--730544f3c51f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-bomb-hoaxes-widen" /><summary type="html">The series of hoax bomb scares sent to several Irish media outlets and European airlines are likely part of a coordinated campaign of disruption, according to the Irish government. Dozens of commercial flights have been targetted by email with threats said to be over and above the typical hoax in specificty. Ireland's broadcaster RTE who's staff evacuated the premises this morning and several Italian airlines, say they received a mesage cliaming to be from a Russian extremist group calling itself the Fighters of the Male State, which denied its implication. France 24's Jean-Emile Jammine speaks to Eric Schouten, founder and CEO of Dyami Security Intelligence.</summary></entry><entry><title>What Trump’s midterms debacle could mean for US support for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b45e2dd6d9f9bfb42e6d5fff11f8ff75d9cdf98fde56d5471aed4e97d9f9e3d1</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T18:49:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-what-trump-s-midterms-debacle-could-mean-for-us-support-for-ukraine--f6b7f8ab35b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-what-trump-s-midterms-debacle-could-mean-for-us-support-for-ukraine" /><summary type="html">The Republican Party's crushing defeat in midterm elections has left Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky optimistic about future support for Kyiv and stronger transatlantic relations. But with US President Donald Trump retaining broad foreign policy powers, the Democratic majority in Congress may have limited scope to bring about substantial change.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe: What we know about the hoax bomb threats disrupting flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d03f57390056b9dbb20287580449ea1f4832098b41da8e458d792d1e5c2f01c8</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T16:59:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-what-we-know-about-the-hoax-bomb-threats-disrupting-flights--25ae3c60f5c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-what-we-know-about-the-hoax-bomb-threats-disrupting-flights" /><summary type="html">Dozens of European flights have been disrupted this week after bomb threats were sent in to various airports, with fighter planes escorting many civilian aircraft after threats were called in mid-flight.</summary></entry><entry><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:247d43c8ba52e7411a22eb9c1987d97810e93e7d57276c4c88cc992bd8e1acbb</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T16:45:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-and-three-sexual-assaults--d4e81a215bb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-and-three-sexual-assaults" /><summary type="html">British comedian Russell Brand was on Thursday, November 5, found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults by a London jury, including for an incident involving a 16-year-old girl. He now faces "significant" prison time, according to the judge.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Trump is a very dangerous person for the world': EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56cea9bbcd3e5c81d30ddbe1ca54ea62c8ea3ff6c6c1579b250e39f2b71a5ac1</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:56:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T16:44:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-trump-is-a-very-dangerous-person-for-the-world-eu-s-former-top-diplomat-josep-borrell--cd806e19d5cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-trump-is-a-very-dangerous-person-for-the-world-eu-s-former-top-diplomat-josep-borrell" /><summary type="html">In an interview with Talking Europe, the EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell reacts to the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections, warning that US President Donald Trump is still "a very dangerous person for the world".</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry></feed>
